// # Models
//
// A model is a struct of an app's package that embeds maago.Model. Its fields are
// the table's columns, and every setting is in the maago:"…" tags. maago
// makemigrations writes the migrations from the models, and maago gen writes
// GetX, InsertX, UpdateX and DeleteX for each.
//
// Field types:
//
//   - int64: BIGINT in PostgreSQL, INTEGER in SQLite.
//   - int32: INTEGER.
//   - bool: BOOLEAN; INTEGER 0 or 1 in SQLite.
//   - float64: DOUBLE PRECISION; REAL in SQLite.
//   - string: TEXT.
//   - time.Time: TIMESTAMPTZ; TEXT in SQLite.
//   - []byte: BYTEA; BLOB in SQLite.
//
// Field tags:
//
//   - max: The most characters of a string: max=200. VARCHAR(n) or a CHECK in the database, a rule in model forms.
//   - unique: A unique constraint on the column.
//   - index: An index on the column. An fk gets one without it.
//   - default: The column's default: default='draft' for a string, default=0, default=true, default=1.5 without quotes.
//   - choices: The values a string may hold, split by /: choices=draft/published. A CHECK, and a select in forms.
//   - label: The name people see, in forms and the admin: label='Title'.
//   - help: A line under the field in forms and the admin: help='Shown in lists'.
//   - fk: The model an int64 ID field refers to: fk=Post, or fk=auth.User for another app's. *int64 for an optional one.
//   - auto: The generated CRUD fills a time.Time with the time: create when inserting, update on every UpdateX, which then compares it (409 on a stale copy). Values: create, update.
//   - admin: hidden leaves the field out of the admin, readonly shows it without an input. Values: hidden, readonly.
//
// Model tags (on the embedded maago.Model):
//
//   - table: The table's name, lowercase SQL: table=posts. Without it, app_model in snake_case.
//   - ordering: The order of the admin's lists: ordering=-PublishedAt, or ordering=(-PublishedAt,Title); - is descending.
//   - unique: A unique constraint over fields: unique=(AuthorID,Slug).
//   - index: An index over fields: index=(Status,PublishedAt).
//   - admin: admin=hidden leaves the model out of the admin. Values: hidden.
//   - admin_list: The admin list's columns: admin_list=(Title,Status).
//   - admin_search: The string fields the admin's search box looks in: admin_search=(Title).
//   - admin_filter: The fields the admin's list filters by, each with a few values (bool, choices, fk): admin_filter=(Status).
//
// Names: [Model], [Opt], [Set], [Ptr], [ErrConflict].
//
// maago doc model has the full text and an example.
//
// # Queries
//
// A query is a file of SQL, queries/name.sql in an app, with a header that names
// the Go function, its result and its parameters. maago gen prepares every
// form of it on a practice database built from the migrations, and writes
// queries_gen.go.
//
// Header lines (-- key: …):
//
//   - name: -- name: Name :kind [Result]: the Go function, what it returns, and the result type.
//   - param: -- param: name[?] type: a value the SQL uses as :name; ? when it may be missing.
//   - column: -- column: name[?] type: the type of a result column the database cannot tell (an expression, an outer join's side); ? when it may be NULL.
//
// Kinds:
//
//   - :one: One row: sql.ErrNoRows when none, maago.ErrManyRows when more.
//   - :many: A slice of rows; none is an empty slice.
//   - :exec: No rows: the number of rows changed (0 is no error).
//
// Names: [DB], [ErrManyRows], [ErrEmptySlice].
//
// maago doc query has the full text and an example.
//
// # Views and routes
//
// A view is a func of an app that takes what it uses and returns a page. The
// app's var Routes lists each route's method, path, name and view, and main
// puts each app's generated App in maago.Config.Apps.
//
// Route methods:
//
//   - GET: maago.GET(path, name, View, options…): reads; its view cannot take maago.Tx.
//   - POST: maago.POST: writes, so its view takes tx maago.Tx (or maago.DB with maago.NoTx).
//   - PUT: maago.PUT: writes, as POST.
//   - PATCH: maago.PATCH: writes, as POST.
//   - DELETE: maago.DELETE: writes, as POST.
//
// Route options (after the view):
//
//   - API: maago.API answers JSON, and errors as RFC 9457 problems; a form error is a 422.
//   - Block: maago.Block("name") renders only that block of the page, for htmx-like partial updates.
//   - NoTx: maago.NoTx lets a writing route run a view that takes maago.DB, outside a transaction: for a write that must stay when the view then fails (a counted login attempt). Give it to every writing route of that view.
//
// In tags (where each field of In comes from):
//
//   - path: path=id reads {id} of the route's path: string, int64 or int32. A value that does not parse is a 404.
//   - query: query=page reads ?page=: string, int64, int32, bool or float64, a pointer to one when it may be missing. A value that does not parse is a 400.
//   - form: form, with no value, reads the request's form (or JSON on an API route) into a form type of the package.
//
// Names: [Routes], [Route], [RouteOption], [GET], [POST], [PUT], [PATCH], [DELETE], [API], [NoTx], [Block], [Result], [Show], [SeeOther], [Status], [Tx], [WithTx], [AfterCommit], [DBFrom], [WithDB].
//
// maago doc view has the full text and an example.
