// # Forms
//
// A form is a struct of an app that embeds maago.Form and has maago.Field[T]
// fields. A view takes it as a field of its In tagged maago:"form"; maago gen
// writes the code that reads and checks each field.
//
// Form field types (maago.Field[T]):
//
//   - string: Text.
//   - int64: A whole number.
//   - int32: A whole number.
//   - float64: A number.
//   - bool: A checkbox: on is true, absent is false.
//   - time.Time: A date or a time, in Config.TimeZone.
//   - maago.File: An uploaded file, in an HTML form only (a multipart one).
//
// Form field tags:
//
//   - label: The name people see: label='Title'. A model form takes the model field's.
//   - help: A line under the input: help='…'.
//   - choices: The values a string may hold, split by /: choices=draft/published.
//   - min: The fewest characters of a string: min=3.
//   - max: The most characters of a string: max=200.
//   - min_value: The smallest number: min_value=1.
//   - max_value: The largest number: max_value=100.
//   - optional: An empty value is no error (a bool never is required). A pointer field of a model is optional in its model form.
//   - accept: The kinds of file a maago.File field takes, split by /: accept=png/jpeg, as the content's first bytes tell: png, jpeg, gif, webp, pdf, zip (zip includes .docx and .xlsx).
//
// Names: [Form], [Field], [Invalid], [InvalidForm], [UniqueError], [File], [Media], [SaveMedia], [OpenMedia], [DeleteMedia], [ServeMedia], [WithMediaDir].
//
// maago doc form has the full text and an example.
